WEBVTT

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:21.918
Dangerous Journey by Alwyn Cox.

00:00:21.978 --> 00:00:29.840
There was forest all around.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.931
all round for hundreds of kilometers.

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:35.481
And there were no roads in the forest.

00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:37.632
There were only tracks.

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:40.522
Two tents stood in a clearing.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:43.193
Two men were standing near the tents.

00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:48.184
The younger man, Manuel, was making coffee on a small stove.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:50.425
He looked up at the sky.

00:00:50.485 --> 00:00:53.956
It's going to rain today, he said.

00:00:54.016 --> 00:00:56.576
I know, replied Leon.

00:00:56.636 --> 00:00:59.380
And the rain will turn the ground into mud.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.194
then we'll never get back to base.

00:01:02.254 --> 00:01:05.254
Four men were working in the forest.

00:01:05.314 --> 00:01:08.385
They were looking for iron and other metals.

00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:13.206
Leon was the boss, and he was angry.

00:01:13.266 --> 00:01:16.346
It was early morning.

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:22.337
Leon and Manuel were ready to leave, but Joe and Pedro were out in the forest.

00:01:22.397 --> 00:01:25.938
They left in the truck two days ago, said Leon.

00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:27.772
They're very late.

00:01:27.831 --> 00:01:30.656
Joe was always making trouble.

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:33.748
He was younger than Leon, and he was clever.

00:01:33.808 --> 00:01:35.950
He wanted to be boss.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:41.633
Manuel poured the coffee into mugs, and the two men drank it slowly.

00:01:41.692 --> 00:01:44.944
Suddenly, they heard the sound of a truck.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.966
They're back, said Manuel.

00:01:48.026 --> 00:01:50.848
The truck came up the rough track.

00:01:50.908 --> 00:01:52.869
It stopped near the tents.

00:01:52.929 --> 00:01:55.398
Joe jumped out.

00:01:55.458 --> 00:01:58.816
He was a big man with red hair.

00:01:58.876 --> 00:02:00.487
He was smiling.

00:02:00.547 --> 00:02:03.899
His smile made Leon more angry.

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:06.541
You're late, said Leon.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.051
Where have you been?

00:02:08.111 --> 00:02:12.574
Hunting, replied Joe, and he held up his rifle.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:15.916
Hunting, Leon shouted angrily.

00:02:15.975 --> 00:02:17.496
That's not your job.

00:02:17.556 --> 00:02:19.438
We haven't time for hunting.

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:23.159
We were away for two days, replied Joe.

00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:24.922
We're not very late.

00:02:24.982 --> 00:02:28.496
I'm the boss here, Leon shouted.

00:02:28.556 --> 00:02:31.287
Joe looked at Leon angrily.

00:02:31.347 --> 00:02:33.528
He was not smiling now.

00:02:33.588 --> 00:02:37.100
We're late, very late, said Leon.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.952
The rain will start soon, and then there will be mud everywhere.

00:02:41.012 --> 00:02:43.034
We must leave now.

00:02:43.093 --> 00:02:49.998
Manuel took down the tents, and Joe and Pedro put the boxes into the truck.

00:02:50.058 --> 00:02:53.132
Hurry, shouted Leon.

00:02:53.192 --> 00:02:54.365
It's 10 o'clock!

00:02:54.425 --> 00:02:57.377
Let's go!

00:02:57.437 --> 00:03:01.990
Soon, everything was in the truck.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.342
Joe sat in the driver's seat.

00:03:04.402 --> 00:03:06.424
Leon sat beside him.

00:03:06.484 --> 00:03:11.508
Manuel and Pedro climbed into the back of the truck.

00:03:11.568 --> 00:03:16.742
Joe started the engine and the journey began.

00:03:16.802 --> 00:03:20.604
They drove easily for the first 20 kilometres.

00:03:20.664 --> 00:03:25.690
Then they came to a stream There was no water here last week.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.781
Pedro shouted to Manuel.

00:03:27.841 --> 00:03:30.082
Look at the water now!

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.052
The stream was full of water.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:38.505
Joe slowed down and drove the truck carefully through the rushing water.

00:03:38.565 --> 00:03:42.507
They crossed the stream and Joe drove faster.

00:03:42.566 --> 00:03:45.268
The rain was now falling heavily.

00:03:45.328 --> 00:03:49.559
The track was very muddy and the truck began to slide.

00:03:49.619 --> 00:03:51.040
Watch out!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.412
Shouted Leon.

00:03:52.472 --> 00:03:53.985
But it was too late.

00:03:54.045 --> 00:03:55.586
The truck stopped.

00:03:55.646 --> 00:03:59.798
The wheels were still turning, but the truck was not moving.

00:03:59.858 --> 00:04:03.811
The wheels were turning round and round in the mud.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:08.363
Leon got out and Pedro and Manuel jumped down.

00:04:08.423 --> 00:04:10.874
Joe sat in the driver's seat.

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.646
Leon looked at the wheels in the mud.

00:04:13.706 --> 00:04:15.727
Then he looked up at Joe.

00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:18.859
It's your fault, he said angrily.

00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:22.472
You were driving too fast.

00:04:22.532 --> 00:04:27.866
Pedro, you cut branches from those trees, ordered Leon.

00:04:27.926 --> 00:04:31.627
And you, Manuel, throw the branches under the wheels.

00:04:31.687 --> 00:04:36.558
Pedro got a large knife out of the truck, and Manuel helped him.

00:04:36.618 --> 00:04:38.569
Leon turned to Joe.

00:04:38.629 --> 00:04:40.939
You, come and help us.

00:04:40.999 --> 00:04:43.230
Joe did not move.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.091
I'm driving the truck, he said.

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:47.711
That's my job.

00:04:47.771 --> 00:04:50.522
I'm boss here, shouted Leon.

00:04:50.582 --> 00:04:52.268
Come and help us.

00:04:52.328 --> 00:04:54.836
Joe did not say anything.

00:04:54.896 --> 00:04:57.049
He did not get out of the truck.

00:04:57.108 --> 00:04:59.550
Leon looked at him angrily.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.072
Then Leon walked away.

00:05:02.132 --> 00:05:06.336
Manuel and Pedro threw branches under the wheels.

00:05:06.395 --> 00:05:08.227
Okay, that's enough.

00:05:08.287 --> 00:05:09.158
Said Leon.

00:05:09.218 --> 00:05:11.340
Let's go.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.592
Joe started the engine again.

00:05:14.652 --> 00:05:17.824
Pedro and Manuel pushed the back of the truck.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:21.090
The wheels turned and the engine roared.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.554
But the truck did not move.

00:05:23.614 --> 00:05:25.236
Push harder!

00:05:25.296 --> 00:05:26.728
Shouted Leon.

00:05:26.787 --> 00:05:29.540
Suddenly, the truck moved forward.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.201
It was out of the mud.

00:05:31.261 --> 00:05:34.364
Pedro and Manuel shouted happily.

00:05:34.424 --> 00:05:38.386
At that moment, a large branch flew up from under a wheel.

00:05:38.446 --> 00:05:40.108
It hit Leon's arm.

00:05:40.168 --> 00:05:42.500
He stepped back and fell in the mud.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.122
Stop the truck!

00:05:44.182 --> 00:05:45.633
Shouted Manuel.

00:05:45.692 --> 00:05:48.614
Leon's hurt!

00:05:48.674 --> 00:05:51.542
My arm!

00:05:51.602 --> 00:05:53.698
Let me see.

00:05:53.758 --> 00:05:55.780
It hurts.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.221
It's broken.

00:05:58.281 --> 00:06:01.464
I'll tie it up.

00:06:01.524 --> 00:06:03.395
That's better.

00:06:03.455 --> 00:06:04.456
Thanks.

00:06:04.516 --> 00:06:06.898
You're lucky it's your left arm.

00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:12.583
Yes, I can use my right.

00:06:12.642 --> 00:06:18.598
At midday, it was still raining heavily.

00:06:18.657 --> 00:06:20.928
The track was covered with mud.

00:06:20.988 --> 00:06:25.000
Joe drove slowly and the truck did not stop again.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.522
They climbed up a steep hill.

00:06:27.582 --> 00:06:30.934
On the other side, the track went down to a river.

00:06:30.994 --> 00:06:33.636
It was the biggest river in the forest.

00:06:33.696 --> 00:06:37.398
This was the last river between the men and their base.

00:06:37.458 --> 00:06:40.680
An old wooden bridge crossed over the river.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.422
They drove down towards the bridge.

00:06:43.482 --> 00:06:44.684
Look!

00:06:44.744 --> 00:06:46.614
Leon shouted to Joe.

00:06:46.674 --> 00:06:48.126
Something's wrong.

00:06:48.186 --> 00:06:49.237
It's the bridge.

00:06:49.296 --> 00:06:50.656
It's broken.

00:06:50.716 --> 00:06:53.106
Joe did not stop the truck.

00:06:53.166 --> 00:06:56.077
He drove down slowly to the bank of the river.

00:06:56.137 --> 00:06:59.018
He drove to the edge of the Broken Bridge.

00:06:59.078 --> 00:07:02.330
Then he stopped.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:06.472
They all got out of the truck.

00:07:06.532 --> 00:07:08.723
They stood in silence.

00:07:08.783 --> 00:07:10.554
Nobody spoke.

00:07:10.614 --> 00:07:14.716
They looked at the Broken Bridge and at the rushing water.

00:07:14.775 --> 00:07:17.176
Pedro spoke first.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:20.294
There is no way across the river now.

00:07:20.354 --> 00:07:22.652
How can we get back to base?

00:07:22.712 --> 00:07:25.474
We must get help, said Leon.

00:07:25.534 --> 00:07:28.346
Pedro, you climb back up the hill.

00:07:28.406 --> 00:07:31.009
Take the radio with you and call base.

00:07:31.069 --> 00:07:34.742
Perhaps they'll hear you and send help.

00:07:34.802 --> 00:07:40.898
Manuel lifted the radio out of the truck and fixed it to Pedro's back.

00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:42.579
Joe stopped them.

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:45.021
It won't work, he said.

00:07:45.081 --> 00:07:46.242
Why not?

00:07:46.302 --> 00:07:47.599
Asked Leon.

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:50.876
It isn't a strong radio," replied Joe.

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:53.106
We're too far away from the base.

00:07:53.166 --> 00:07:55.697
No one will hear us from this side of the river.

00:07:55.757 --> 00:07:58.408
We must cross the river by ourselves.

00:07:58.468 --> 00:08:00.659
We can't, said Leon.

00:08:00.719 --> 00:08:02.039
We must get help.

00:08:02.099 --> 00:08:05.380
We can't get help from here, said Joe.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.561
We must cross the river first.

00:08:07.621 --> 00:08:09.421
Then we can get help.

00:08:09.481 --> 00:08:12.752
But how do we get across, asked Leon?

00:08:12.812 --> 00:08:14.093
It's too dangerous.

00:08:14.153 --> 00:08:15.748
Look at the water.

00:08:15.808 --> 00:08:20.646
The rain was still falling heavily, and the water was rising.

00:08:20.706 --> 00:08:23.528
I have a plan, said Joe.

00:08:23.588 --> 00:08:26.742
Leon looked at Joe and smiled.

00:08:26.802 --> 00:08:29.854
You're clever, Joe, Leon said.

00:08:29.914 --> 00:08:33.446
You always have plans, but they never work.

00:08:33.506 --> 00:08:37.329
Let's listen to Joe's plan, said Manuel.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:40.682
We can use the boat, said Joe.

00:08:40.742 --> 00:08:42.276
Leon laughed.

00:08:42.336 --> 00:08:43.848
Don't be stupid.

00:08:43.908 --> 00:08:46.089
The boat's too small for four people.

00:08:46.149 --> 00:08:47.649
And look at the rushing water.

00:08:47.709 --> 00:08:49.480
It will carry the boat away.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.281
But we've got a rope, said Joe.

00:08:52.341 --> 00:08:54.541
We can tie the rope to the boat.

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:58.332
With luck, the water will carry the boat to the other side.

00:08:58.392 --> 00:09:01.263
We can try it, said Pedro.

00:09:01.323 --> 00:09:04.104
It won't work, said Leon.

00:09:04.164 --> 00:09:06.794
It will work, said Joe.

00:09:06.854 --> 00:09:09.746
Look, I'll show you.

00:09:09.806 --> 00:09:14.400
We tie a rope to this end of the bridge.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:20.232
Then we tie the rope to the boat and carry it up the river.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:25.684
Two of us get into the boat and push it into the river.

00:09:25.744 --> 00:09:30.236
We paddle hard to get to the other side.

00:09:30.296 --> 00:09:34.939
We tie the rope to the other end of the bridge.

00:09:34.999 --> 00:09:40.425
One of us pulls the rope and brings the boat back.

00:09:40.485 --> 00:09:46.212
It won't work, Leon said, but we can try it.

00:09:46.272 --> 00:09:48.974
I'll go first, Joe said.

00:09:49.034 --> 00:09:50.685
It's my plan.

00:09:50.744 --> 00:09:54.057
No, let me go, said Pedro.

00:09:54.117 --> 00:09:55.868
I am stronger.

00:09:55.928 --> 00:09:59.040
You can both go, said Leon.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.732
Pedro, you stay on the other side.

00:10:01.791 --> 00:10:05.934
Joe, you bring the boat back, and then you can take Manuel.

00:10:05.994 --> 00:10:08.396
Then you can come back again for me.

00:10:08.456 --> 00:10:10.871
Good, Joe said.

00:10:10.931 --> 00:10:13.216
Pedro, you bring the radio.

00:10:13.276 --> 00:10:15.968
You can use it on the other side of the river.

00:10:16.028 --> 00:10:20.580
Pedro got the rubber boat out of the truck and pumped it up.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.482
Leon helped him with his right arm.

00:10:23.542 --> 00:10:26.394
There was a long rope in the back of the truck.

00:10:26.454 --> 00:10:29.216
Joe tied it to the broken bridge.

00:10:29.276 --> 00:10:33.558
Manuel tied the other end of the rope to the rubber boat.

00:10:33.618 --> 00:10:36.510
It's a long rope, Leon said.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.128
It'll be all right.

00:10:38.188 --> 00:10:40.116
Harry said Joe.

00:10:40.176 --> 00:10:43.818
The water is rising quickly.

00:10:43.878 --> 00:10:47.970
Joe and Pedro carried the boat.

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.022
Manuel and Leon walked behind them.

00:10:51.082 --> 00:10:53.204
Manuel held the boat.

00:10:53.264 --> 00:10:56.536
Joe and Pedro climbed in.

00:10:56.596 --> 00:11:01.748
The rushing water took the boat into the middle of the river.

00:11:01.808 --> 00:11:05.000
The boat crossed to the other side.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.420
It came near the bridge.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.749
Joe held on.

00:11:09.809 --> 00:11:13.140
Pedro climbed out of the boat.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:18.762
Pedro tied the rope to a piece of the bridge.

00:11:18.822 --> 00:11:23.102
Pedro stayed on the far side of the river.

00:11:23.162 --> 00:11:29.174
Joe pulled hard on the rope and the boat slowly came back to Leon and Manuel.

00:11:29.234 --> 00:11:31.264
You get in now, Manuel?

00:11:31.324 --> 00:11:32.365
Said Leon.

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:34.070
I'm going last.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.575
No, you're not.

00:11:35.635 --> 00:11:36.946
Manuel replied.

00:11:37.006 --> 00:11:38.598
Your arm is broken.

00:11:38.658 --> 00:11:40.820
You can't get into the boat alone.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.140
You need help.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.662
I'll help you.

00:11:43.722 --> 00:11:46.565
Manuel is right, said Joe.

00:11:46.624 --> 00:11:48.806
You need help, Leon.

00:11:48.866 --> 00:11:52.030
Manuel helped Leon into the boat.

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:56.994
He sat down in the boat, and Joe pulled hard on the rope.

00:11:57.054 --> 00:11:59.596
Trouble came suddenly.

00:11:59.656 --> 00:12:02.268
Joe and Leon were in the middle of the river.

00:12:02.328 --> 00:12:04.438
Leon saw the tree first.

00:12:04.498 --> 00:12:07.810
The rushing water was pulling it down the river.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.192
Look out!

00:12:09.252 --> 00:12:10.772
Leon shouted.

00:12:10.832 --> 00:12:12.684
Joe looked round.

00:12:12.743 --> 00:12:16.506
At that moment, the branches of the tree hit the boat.

00:12:16.566 --> 00:12:18.637
Joe held onto the rope.

00:12:18.698 --> 00:12:22.220
His feet slipped and the boat moved away from him.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.971
Hold onto the rope!

00:12:24.031 --> 00:12:25.552
Leon shouted.

00:12:25.612 --> 00:12:27.734
But Joe did not listen.

00:12:27.794 --> 00:12:32.807
He let go of the rope and swam towards the rubber boat.

00:12:32.867 --> 00:12:37.590
Joe was a good swimmer and he soon reached the boat.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:42.172
He held it tightly and kicked his legs hard in the water.

00:12:42.232 --> 00:12:45.024
The boat moved away from the tree.

00:12:45.084 --> 00:12:46.294
Good!

00:12:46.354 --> 00:12:47.876
Joe shouted to Leon.

00:12:47.936 --> 00:12:49.556
The boat's free.

00:12:49.616 --> 00:12:51.338
Leave the boat!

00:12:51.398 --> 00:12:52.578
Shouted Leon.

00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:54.339
Save yourself!

00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:56.410
Joe did not listen.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:59.652
He held the boat and kicked his legs.

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:03.844
A few moments later, Joe heard a loud noise.

00:13:03.904 --> 00:13:05.335
What's that?

00:13:05.395 --> 00:13:07.055
He asked Leon.

00:13:07.116 --> 00:13:08.906
It's a waterfall.

00:13:08.966 --> 00:13:10.296
Replied Leon.

00:13:10.356 --> 00:13:12.686
The water will pull the boat over.

00:13:12.746 --> 00:13:13.917
Leave the boat.

00:13:13.977 --> 00:13:15.497
Save yourself.

00:13:15.557 --> 00:13:16.807
Look.

00:13:16.867 --> 00:13:18.197
Shouted Joe.

00:13:18.257 --> 00:13:20.608
There's a rock in front of us.

00:13:20.668 --> 00:13:22.348
We must reach it.

00:13:22.408 --> 00:13:24.258
Don't be a fool.

00:13:24.318 --> 00:13:25.319
Said Leon.

00:13:25.379 --> 00:13:26.679
Save yourself.

00:13:26.739 --> 00:13:28.609
You can't save me.

00:13:28.669 --> 00:13:31.400
The water rushed round the boat.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.036
It was pulling them towards the waterfall.

00:13:34.096 --> 00:13:36.382
Joe kicked his legs harder.

00:13:36.442 --> 00:13:39.083
The boat moved quickly towards the rock.

00:13:39.143 --> 00:13:40.383
Get ready!

00:13:40.443 --> 00:13:41.614
Shouted Joe.

00:13:41.674 --> 00:13:43.364
Jump for the rock!

00:13:43.424 --> 00:13:46.276
Leon was ready.

00:13:46.336 --> 00:13:51.318
The boat came near the rock and Leon jumped.

00:13:51.378 --> 00:13:55.429
Joe let go of the boat and swam to the rock.

00:13:55.489 --> 00:13:58.240
The two men lay on the rock.

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:01.709
For a few minutes they did not say anything.

00:14:01.769 --> 00:14:05.760
Then Leon turned and smiled at Joe.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.322
Joe had saved his life.

00:14:08.382 --> 00:14:11.754
We're not safe yet, Joe shouted.

00:14:11.815 --> 00:14:15.217
The rain has stopped, but the water is still rising.

00:14:15.277 --> 00:14:17.850
It'll cover the rock in an hour or two.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.530
Joe was right.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.603
There was water all round the two men.

00:14:22.663 --> 00:14:26.156
In front of them, the water dropped over the waterfall.

00:14:26.216 --> 00:14:29.168
Behind them, there was the broken bridge.

00:14:29.228 --> 00:14:31.843
We must get help, said Leon.

00:14:31.903 --> 00:14:33.466
But how?

00:14:33.526 --> 00:14:36.037
Pedro, replied Joe.

00:14:36.097 --> 00:14:37.307
He can help us.

00:14:37.367 --> 00:14:41.658
He's got the radio.

00:14:41.718 --> 00:14:47.529
Pedro was waiting on the far side of the river.

00:14:47.589 --> 00:14:49.659
He watched Joe and Leon.

00:14:49.719 --> 00:14:51.650
They climbed onto the rock.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.320
They were safe.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:56.971
They won't be safe for long, thought Pedro.

00:14:57.031 --> 00:14:59.696
I must call base and get help.

00:14:59.756 --> 00:15:02.792
Pedro climbed up the hill behind him.

00:15:02.852 --> 00:15:05.414
He walked quickly for half an hour.

00:15:05.474 --> 00:15:09.368
At the top of the hill, he climbed onto a high rock.

00:15:09.428 --> 00:15:13.632
He took the radio off his back and pulled out the aerial.

00:15:13.692 --> 00:15:16.414
Pedro spoke into the radio.

00:15:16.474 --> 00:15:19.556
PX-75 calling base.

00:15:19.616 --> 00:15:22.670
PX-75 calling base.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.344
He waited and listened.

00:15:25.404 --> 00:15:28.127
PX-75 calling base.

00:15:28.187 --> 00:15:30.878
PX-75 calling base.

00:15:30.938 --> 00:15:33.128
There was no reply.

00:15:33.188 --> 00:15:36.079
PX-75 calling base.

00:15:36.139 --> 00:15:40.880
PX-75 calling base.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:45.610
Philip was sitting at the control desk.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.651
He was listening to the radio.

00:15:47.711 --> 00:15:50.901
PX-75 was Leon's number.

00:15:50.961 --> 00:15:53.622
Philip turned the dials of the radio.

00:15:53.682 --> 00:15:55.879
The voice became clearer.

00:15:55.939 --> 00:15:59.757
Hello PX-75, said Philip.

00:15:59.817 --> 00:16:01.107
This is Bass.

00:16:01.167 --> 00:16:03.548
What's your message, Ova?

00:16:03.608 --> 00:16:07.388
Hello Bass, PX-75 here.

00:16:07.448 --> 00:16:08.989
Pedro speaking.

00:16:09.049 --> 00:16:10.499
Can you hear me?

00:16:10.559 --> 00:16:12.679
Loud and clear, Pedro.

00:16:12.739 --> 00:16:15.070
What's your message, Ova?

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:18.240
We're in trouble, said Pedro.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:21.871
The bridge over the river Santano is broken.

00:16:21.931 --> 00:16:25.808
Joe and Leon are on a rock in the middle of the river.

00:16:25.868 --> 00:16:28.036
They are above the waterfall.

00:16:28.096 --> 00:16:29.596
Can you send help?

00:16:29.656 --> 00:16:30.706
Over.

00:16:30.766 --> 00:16:35.168
River Sandano, near Bridge, above Waterfall.

00:16:35.228 --> 00:16:37.698
Okay Pedro, help is coming.

00:16:37.758 --> 00:16:40.208
Over.

00:16:40.268 --> 00:16:45.200
Pedro climbed down the hill to the Broken Bridge.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.571
Manuel was waiting on the other side of the river.

00:16:48.631 --> 00:16:52.394
Pedro shouted and Manuel waved.

00:16:52.454 --> 00:16:54.998
Both men looked down the river.

00:16:55.058 --> 00:16:59.632
The water was rising fast, and the rock looked very small now.

00:16:59.692 --> 00:17:03.555
On the rock, Joe was holding Leon in his arms.

00:17:03.614 --> 00:17:06.276
Leon's arm was covered in blood.

00:17:06.337 --> 00:17:09.848
His eyes were closed, and he did not move.

00:17:09.908 --> 00:17:12.501
Then Joe heard the noise.

00:17:12.561 --> 00:17:14.022
A helicopter.

00:17:14.082 --> 00:17:16.814
It was high above the broken bridge.

00:17:16.873 --> 00:17:18.605
A helicopter!

00:17:18.665 --> 00:17:19.756
Joe shouted.

00:17:19.816 --> 00:17:21.456
Leon, look!

00:17:21.516 --> 00:17:25.728
but Leon's eyes were closed and he said nothing.

00:17:25.788 --> 00:17:28.800
The helicopter was soon over the rock.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.842
A rope was lowered and Joe held it.

00:17:31.902 --> 00:17:34.384
Then he tied it round Leon.

00:17:34.444 --> 00:17:39.277
Joe held Leon with one hand and he held the rope with the other.

00:17:39.337 --> 00:17:46.694
Slowly the two men were lifted in the air.

00:17:46.754 --> 00:17:53.100
Leon woke up slowly.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.340
He was still half asleep.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.042
Where am I?

00:17:57.102 --> 00:17:58.432
He asked.

00:17:58.492 --> 00:18:02.114
Then he remembered the rock and the helicopter.

00:18:02.174 --> 00:18:03.744
And Joe.

00:18:03.804 --> 00:18:07.636
Joe, he shouted out, where's Joe?

00:18:07.696 --> 00:18:10.237
Don't worry, said a voice.

00:18:10.297 --> 00:18:12.248
I'm not dead yet.

00:18:12.308 --> 00:18:16.370
Leon opened his eyes fully and saw Joe.

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.338
Joe was smiling.

00:18:18.398 --> 00:18:21.656
Pedro and Manuel was standing next to him.

00:18:21.716 --> 00:18:24.578
The four men were in a hut at base.

00:18:24.638 --> 00:18:29.181
Leon was lying in bed, and his arm was in plaster.

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:33.754
You'll feel better in a few days, Leon, said Joe.

00:18:33.814 --> 00:18:36.666
I feel better now, said Leon.

00:18:36.726 --> 00:18:38.536
But I need a drink.

00:18:38.596 --> 00:18:39.937
Water?

00:18:39.997 --> 00:18:41.438
asked Manuel.

00:18:41.498 --> 00:18:44.976
No, not water, replied Leon.

00:18:45.036 --> 00:18:49.166
I don't want to see water again, not for a long time.

00:18:49.226 --> 00:18:55.282
And they all laughed.

00:18:55.342 --> 00:19:03.128
Dangerous Journey was read by Stephen Pacey.

00:19:03.188 --> 00:19:08.434
And the recording produced by James Richardson at Studio AVP London.

